WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:09.700
Cut a neuron's axon close to the cell body, and one of its dendrites can grow out as

2
00:00:09.700 --> 00:00:15.440
a new axon. Cut the axon farther away, and the old axon simply regrows.

3
00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:18.680
So an axon is not a permanent label.

4
00:00:19.420 --> 00:00:24.040
What decides which process becomes the axon, and what keeps it that way?

5
00:00:24.883 --> 00:00:31.803
Start in a dish. A rat hippocampal neuron grows several short neurites, and they all

6
00:00:31.803 --> 00:00:37.503
look alike. After a day or two, one neurite starts to grow much faster than the

7
00:00:37.503 --> 00:00:40.623
rest. That neurite becomes the axon.

8
00:00:41.403 --> 00:00:46.183
A neurite tends to win once it is about 10 micrometres longer than the others.

9
00:00:46.843 --> 00:00:48.663
The choice behaves like a race.

10
00:00:49.617 --> 00:00:53.497
A race with one winner needs two kinds of feedback.

11
00:00:54.557 --> 00:00:58.817
Positive feedback in the leader makes it grow faster the more it grows.

12
00:00:59.717 --> 00:01:03.577
A lipid called PIP3 builds up at its tip.

13
00:01:04.697 --> 00:01:10.177
Blocking PI3-kinase is reported to stop any neurite from becoming an axon.

14
00:01:11.337 --> 00:01:13.837
Negative feedback holds the others back.

15
00:01:14.597 --> 00:01:16.457
How it does that is less settled.

16
00:01:17.417 --> 00:01:21.037
Look at the growth cone, the moving tip of the leader.

17
00:01:21.837 --> 00:01:24.557
Its actin network is looser than in its siblings.

18
00:01:25.677 --> 00:01:31.377
Loosened actin is proposed to let microtubules push in, and the microtubules there

19
00:01:31.377 --> 00:01:36.997
are more stable. Loosen the actin in a chosen neurite, or stabilize its

20
00:01:36.997 --> 00:01:40.717
microtubules, and that neurite can become the axon.

21
00:01:41.567 --> 00:01:44.727
Once chosen, the axon has to be held.

22
00:01:45.567 --> 00:01:51.287
Near the cell body, a scaffold called ankyrin G builds the axon initial segment.

23
00:01:51.847 --> 00:01:53.047
It works as a gate.

24
00:01:53.827 --> 00:01:57.707
Lower ankyrin G in a mature neuron, and the segment falls apart.

25
00:01:58.467 --> 00:02:02.507
A dendrite protein called MAP2 spreads into the axon.

26
00:02:02.887 --> 00:02:05.427
The axon begins to look like a dendrite.

27
00:02:06.167 --> 00:02:07.907
Now return to the cut.

28
00:02:08.827 --> 00:02:14.067
Leave a stump shorter than 35 micrometres, and no process is clearly ahead.

29
00:02:14.787 --> 00:02:18.067
It is like the first race again, and a dendrite can win it.

30
00:02:18.567 --> 00:02:21.467
Leave a longer stump, and the old axon regrows.

31
00:02:22.387 --> 00:02:26.147
Keep this rule. An axon is a state the cell holds.

32
00:02:26.767 --> 00:02:30.527
If enough of it is lost, that state can pass to another process.
